@page "/"

<PageTitle>Order Aggregation Service</PageTitle>

<h1>Order Aggregation Service</h1>

<p class="lead">
    A .NET 10 service that accepts batches of order lines over HTTP and accumulates the ordered
    quantity per product, ready to be handed over to a downstream system.
</p>

<div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-3 g-3 my-3">
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title h5">Dashboard</h2>
                <p class="card-text">Live service status and the current aggregate.</p>
                <a class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" href="dashboard">Open dashboard</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title h5">OpenAPI</h2>
                <p class="card-text">Machine readable description of the REST API.</p>
                <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm" href="openapi/v1.json" target="_blank">
                    View document
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title h5">Health</h2>
                <p class="card-text">Readiness probe used by container orchestrators.</p>
                <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm" href="health" target="_blank">Check health</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Submit an order batch</h2>

<p>
    <code>POST /api/orders</code> takes a JSON array of order lines. Every line needs a non-empty
    <code>productId</code> and a <code>quantity</code> greater than zero.
</p>

<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3"><code>curl -X POST http://localhost:5212/api/orders \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '[{"productId":"456","quantity":5},{"productId":"789","quantity":42}]'</code></pre>

<p>
    The service answers with <code>202 Accepted</code> and a receipt describing what was taken in.
    Read the running totals back from <code>GET /api/orders/aggregates</code>.
</p>
